<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">House of Auersperg</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Auersperg family</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The House of Auersperg is an Austrian noble family originating in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/carniola">Carniola</a>, at the castle of Auersperg (Turjak) in present-day <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/slovenia">Slovenia</a>. Its members served the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/habsburg-dynasty">Habsburgs</a> as soldiers and statesmen, and in 1653 the line of Johann Weikhard von Auersperg was raised to princely rank. In 1654 the family received the Silesian Duchy of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ziebice">Münsterberg</a>. Later members included the Austrian prime ministers Karl and Adolf von Auersperg.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/house-of-auersperg.jpg" alt="House of Auersperg" width="320" height="400" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Auersperg-Fuersten-Wappen.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
